    "durationMs": 148361,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified. I built it with Express 4.21.2 (pinned exactly), `pg` as the persistence layer, and `node-pg-migrate` for migrations.\n\n**What's in place:**\n- `start.sh` — applies pending migrations, then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`; reads `DATABASE_URL` from the environment (nothing hard-coded)\n- `migrations/001-create-links.js` — creates the `links` table with unique `code`, `url`, `clicks`, and creation ordering via `bigserial` id\n- `src/app.js` — all routes with validation: absolute http/https URL with host required, codes must match 4–20 `[A-Za-z0-9_-]`, auto-generated 8-char codes with collision retry\n\n**Verified against every requirement:** 201 with `{code, url, clicks: 0}` and URL returned unchanged, 409 on duplicate custom code, 200/404 on `GET /links/{code}`, 302 redirect with exact `Location` and exactly one click increment per request (atomic `UPDATE ... RETURNING`), ascending-order list with `items`/`total`, and 422 JSON errors for malformed JSON, bad/missing URLs, and invalid codes. I also confirmed data and click counts survive a restart, migrations are skipped once applied, `start.sh` works from any cwd, and the database is truncated clean for the test run."
  }
